# Palm A6 Battery Controller Configuration
#

config BATTERY_PALM_A6
	tristate "Palm A6 battery controller"
	depends on I2C && OF
	help
	  Support for the Palm A6 battery controller used in the HP TouchPad
	  (Tenderloin). The A6 is a TI MSP430 companion MCU that exposes
	  battery state (voltage, current, temperature, capacity, coulomb
	  counter) over I2C; this driver makes that state available through
	  the standard power_supply class.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
	  will be called a6_battery.

config BATTERY_PALM_A6_I2C_SINGLE_BYTE
	bool "Use single-byte I2C reads for A6 register access"
	depends on BATTERY_PALM_A6
	help
	  Use single-byte I2C read transactions on every A6 register access
	  instead of the chained N-byte read the A6 firmware normally
	  expects. This is a workaround for I2C bus masters or PMICs that
	  cannot generate (or correctly handle) a repeated-START sequence
	  followed by an N-byte read, so the driver issues N independent
	  single-byte reads instead.

	  Only required on the legacy Palm PMIC-attached I2C bus topology.
	  If unsure, say N.

config BATTERY_PALM_A6_A2A_COMM
	tristate "Palm A6 legacy A2A comm interface (Tap-to-Share)"
	depends on BATTERY_PALM_A6 && AUXILIARY_BUS
	help
	  Re-exposes the legacy /dev/a6_N character device and
	  /sys/class/misc/a6_N/regs/ sysfs attributes that the
	  original webOS Tap-to-Share userspace (tap2shared) consumes.

	  This interface is NOT for upstream submission; it exists only
	  to keep legacy webOS userspace running on a mainline kernel.
	  Modern webOS / LuneOS userspace does not consume this
	  interface - they go through the standard power_supply class.

	  Say M here unless you intend to boot legacy webOS / use
	  Tap-to-Share between Palm/HP devices.
